    "body": "The recorded temporal-descent Context displacement `self_transition[3610]` q−1→−2 left the previously inspected Prefix/Source/final-U actions unchanged, but earlier consumed Context events were unmeasured. This diagnostic closes that complete-path question by reusing 16 exact compatible control traces and capturing only two missing task steps, with complete guarded admission/step coverage and full native baseline parity.\n\nThe measured 2,137 transition inputs contain four task and 50 control frozen-input action crossings. The first task crossing changes action23→62 at earlier consumed token349; this justifies one declared coherent native Source/U-bound finite contrast after delivery. It does not establish propagated candidate states, improved pools/objective or replies. No gradient, rerank, optimizer, finite candidate or autoregressive rollout runs; serving gains no special case.\n\nValidation: measured source1e1c6d4bb699b17eb21c929a0f5eaa48ea151ad0 passes scoped formatting,71 actual Rust example tests and CUDA-feature release build. Independent mathematical/adversarial source reviews pass. Independent saved audit recomputes all-family integer scores/ties, synchronous H4 composition, all scopes/U suffixes, both complete fresh native snapshots and all2,137 margins: PASS. Five complete-file Rust BLAKE3 verifications pass separately. Final exact-head reviews/checks are posted before queue entry.\n\nExact source/bin/config/reviews were privately preserved and freshly downloaded before the captures at HFc1a90e40eac4e2c74804fb776375b066aacb11cd. Complete result/audit is freshly verified at HFfc5e6dbf02f39250f37173edaff97804c8649f33; structured public evidence and current state bind the exact identities, scope and next causal task. Existing558870s cumulative projection retained without increment; native host arithmetic on the admitted pod, GPU model work NOT_RUN/manual shared runner UNVERIFIED. The previous8/512 result keeps its scope and the exact unbudgeted useful-model goal remains active.\n\nReferences #820.\n",
